{"id": "q_battle_with_the_wolf_and_aftermath_1", "question": "When the council-chamber fight ends, where does that leave the Wolf-dead, fled, what?", "answer": "TL;DR: The Wolf ends the council-chamber fight dead—specifically **“Decapitated; head removed from body”**—despite earlier attempts to flee invisibly.\n\nThere are conflicting OBSERVED states for **the Wolf**:  \n- Earlier in the fight, he **“Downed an Invisibility Potion,” “Disappeared (became invisible),”** and was **“Attempting to escape through a secret passage while invisible.”**  \n- However, a later OBSERVED physical condition states **“Decapitated; head removed from body.”**\n\nBecause death is a terminal outcome, this supersedes prior escape attempts. So even if he briefly fled or turned invisible, the final, current state is that he was killed in the chamber.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- Role: Central adversary in the council chamber battle  \n- Tactics: Illusory duplicates; invisibility; escape via secret passage  \n- Alignment: Cultist, saboteur of the council  \n- Mental State: Desperate, regretful, begging for release  \n- Final Condition: **“Decapitated; head removed from body”** (current, overriding state)", "has_error": false, "retrieval": {"enabled": true, "top_k": 30, "pre_filter_count": 732, "post_filter_count": 30, "duration_ms": 25, "top_5": [["ent_arcane_locks", 1.8], ["ent_the_wolf", 1.791], ["ent_magic_pulse_alarms", 1.689], ["ent_battle_with_the_wolf_in_the_council_chamber", 1.6], ["ent_doors_lock_magically", 1.593]], "selected_entity_ids": ["ent_arcane_locks", "ent_the_wolf", "ent_magic_pulse_alarms", "ent_battle_with_the_wolf_in_the_council_chamber", "ent_doors_lock_magically", "ent_speak_with_dead", "ent_escape_tunnel", "ent_dead_horse", "ent_magical_alarm_system", "ent_fight", "ent_city_council", "ent_corrupted_guard_patrol", "ent_thalia", "ent_citizenry", "ent_the_city", "ent_branching_paths_after_the_fight", "ent_heavy_iron_shutters", "ent_grobnok_the_goblin", "ent_necromancer", "ent