{"id": "q_wolf_status", "question": "End of Session 12: is the Wolf alive, dead, still corrupted-what's his state?", "answer": "TL;DR: The Wolf is dead at the end of Session 12—**“Decapitated; head removed from body”**—and there’s no evidence the corruption was cured before death.\n\nKey Attributes:\n- physical_condition (OBSERVED): **“Decapitated; head removed from body”**; previously had **“oily sheen to his eyes.”**\n- mental_state (OBSERVED): desperate, **begging to be killed**, regretful\n- operational_status (OBSERVED): was attempting escape while invisible before being stopped\n- faction/alignment (OBSERVED): cultist; betrayer of Mirathorn\n\nExplanation:\nThe most current and terminal outcome is the Wolf being **“Decapitated; head removed from body”**, reinforced by Bonogo’s action of removing the head. This overrides earlier states like invisibility or escape. The **“oily sheen to his eyes”** indicates he was still corrupted prior to death, and there is no stated resolution of that condition. Combined with his pleas (begging for death), it suggests he died while still under that corrupting influence.", "has_error": false, "retrieval": {"enabled": true, "top_k": 30, "pre_filter_count": 732, "post_filter_count": 30, "duration_ms": 25, "top_5": [["ent_the_wolf", 1.8276], ["ent_guards", 1.7858], ["ent_speak_with_dead", 1.5514], ["ent_dead_horse", 1.5454], ["ent_battle_with_the_wolf_in_the_council_chamber", 1.4]], "selected_entity_ids": ["ent_the_wolf", "ent_guards", "ent_speak_with_dead", "ent_dead_horse", "ent_battle_with_the_wolf_in_the_council_chamber", "ent_bonogo", "ent_stafl", "ent_stone_bridge", "ent_dead_horses_owner", "ent_session_13_the_meaty_and_the_dead", "ent_thalia", "ent_guard", "ent_meat_flies", "ent_sprite", "ent_necromancer", "ent_shepherds_flock_cultists", "ent_bomb", "ent_karsemine_the_tiefling_ranger", "ent_ephanna_the_kenku_warlock", "ent_the_cult", "ent_dagger", "ent_baergrom_the_dwarf_fighter", "ent_the_city", "ent_25_gold_pieces", "ent_